elaine_cs: Drafting a short customer-facing runbook for handling bursty streaming + batching across clients — want quick reviews. TL;DR: advise customers on client debounce, client-side batching, cache key hygiene, and signals to watch for renewal risk.

diego_eng: Thanks — link to draft: https://docs.google.com/mock-runbook (please treat as WIP). Can we add a small section on client-side debounce + jitter? Many customers trigger spikes from UI events.

elaine_cs: Good call. Thinking guidance: 100–300ms debounce on typing events, add 10–30% jitter to avoid thundering herd. Suggest server header for graceful backpressure: X-RWQ-Backoff. Draft snippet: ```http
POST /v1/stream
Headers: X-RWQ-Backoff: 1
```

sam_platform: Also include recommended cache-key shape: customer_id|route|prompt_hash|model_variant. TTL recommendations: conversation prefix cache ~30s, short-term rerank caches ~5m, static embeddings 24h. Call out when to use per-tenant caches vs global.

mira_sre: Monitoring/playbook additions: watch 95th token latency, error-rate by client_id, and request-per-minute trend. If we see a sustained 20% jump in 95p latency or 10%+ error-rate in 24h, create a high-touch CSM alert. Add runbook step: triage in Console -> traces -> sample tokens.

elaine_cs: Proposed renewal-signal heuristic (for enablement/escalation): >=3 sev-2 issues in 14d OR a 20% regression in success-rate on a customer eval suite (14d window) => escalate to CSM + AM. Add tags: billing-impact, latency-impact.

ops-bot: Deploy note: new doc pushed to /runbooks/customer-facing/streaming_debounce.md by @elaine_cs at 2025-06-15T10:12Z :white_check_mark:

diego_eng: One more thing — include sample client pseudocode for exponential backoff on 429/5xx with cap 4 retries. Pasteable snippet: ```js
async function sendWithBackoff(req){
  for(let i=0;i<4;i++){
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if(res.status===429 || res.status>=500){
      await sleep(2**i * 200 + jitter());
      continue;
    }
    return res;
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```

elaine_cs: :thumbsup: I'll add a short troubleshooting checklist for CS calls: (1) confirm client debounce + batching enabled, (2) verify cache-key shape and TTL, (3) check model pinned/versioned, (4) review Console traces & sample tokens, (5) confirm no recent deploys that match incident time.

sam_platform: LGTM. Small wording ask: replace 'renewal-risk > 0.5' language with 'renewal-risk score >= 0.5' and add link to the scoring rubric (internal).

elaine_cs: Done — updated doc and added rubric link. Anyone want to draft canned CSM outreach lines? Quick ones would help on rotation.

mira_sre: Drafted two short lines, drop-in ready: 1) "We're seeing elevated latency on your account; we've applied a temporary routing fix and would like to run a 10-minute test to validate." 2) "To reduce error spikes, enabling client-side batching with this snippet will help — happy to pair on a quick change." I'll add to the doc under 'CS outreach'.

elaine_cs: Perfect, merging and scheduling an enablement show-and-tell next week. Thanks everyone!

jenny_csm: Adding one last note — can we include a short FAQ entry: 'Will batching change model quality?' Answer: small batched prompts may change latency but shouldn't change model outputs if prompt order and context are preserved; include a note to re-run the customer's eval set post-change.
